course: dictionary
lesson: 392
title: Apology: saying sorry well
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An apology is words that say you are sorry for something you did wrong, or for hurting someone. A good apology says sorry, names what you did, and tries to make things right. «The quickest road back is a full, honest apology with no "but".» The word "but" spoils it, because it makes the sorry sound like an excuse.
explain: Context shows you which meaning you need. «When someone hurts you in front of others, it can be fair to ask for an apology in front of the same people.» Here an apology is a real sorry for hurt. But in school you may read "apologies for absence", which is a message saying someone cannot come. The words around it tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Some useful phrases: make an apology, say an apology, owe someone an apology, accept an apology, and a letter of apology. To owe someone an apology means you did wrong and should say sorry. To accept an apology means you choose to forgive. «A real apology and a simple agreement can turn a quarrel with a neighbour into peace.»
fact: An apology means words that say you are sorry.
fact: «Apologies» can also be a message saying someone cannot come, as in "apologies for absence".
fact: A good apology does not have a "but" in it.
fact: Saying sorry does not wipe out what you did, but a real apology can still fix old hurts.
fact: «The Mole's apology» shows a good sorry: he says he is «very sorry indeed for my foolish and ungrateful conduct».
exercise: «I am very sorry indeed for my foolish and ungrateful conduct.» What is this? | A kind of cake | A loud noise | *Words saying sorry for something wrong | A game played outdoors
exercise: The school sends "apologies for absence" about Mia. What does apologies mean here? | A type of cake | Loud shouting | *A message saying someone cannot come | Words saying sorry for hurting someone
exercise: «Having changed does not wipe out responsibility for what you did before; an apology can still fix old hurts.» What can an apology do? | Wipe out all your responsibility | Make the rain stop | Stop the clock | *Fix old hurts
test: Which phrase means you did wrong and should say sorry? | Owe someone a pound | Make a mess | *Owe someone an apology | Hold a meeting
test: Which is the best kind of apology? | A loud shout across the playground | A note with no name on it | A quick mumble with "but it wasn't me" | *A full, honest apology with no "but"
exam: Ella says a letter of apology is always sent by a grown-up. Is she right, and how do you know? | *Ella is right, because only grown-ups write letters | No, because letters cannot say sorry | No, a child can write a letter of apology too, because the word means a letter saying sorry | Yes, because apologies are only for adults
